  ('2dc44a4f-a6c0-46f7-bc0a-884b7ba26adb', '36JD02', NULL, 'Double Check Detector Assembly: For Water Media, Low Health Hazard, 33°F 110°F, Plastic, CFM', 'Watts double check backflow preventer detectors replace existing valves of the same brand.', NULL, '805951e5-11f5-4b68-9916-30f4db4b07c5', 'https://static.grainger.com/rp/s/is/image/Grainger/e711278038cf2e3b1e286d06e06dd__XDFI_v1', '4191507.00', NULL, 'in_stock', NULL, 'f', '36JD02', '{"Flow": "525 gpm", "Valve Series": "774DCDA", "Body Material": "Stainless Steel", "Overall Length": "37 in", "Connection Type": "Flange", "Media Temp. Range": "33  Degrees F 110  Degrees F", "Nominal Valve Size": "2-1/2 in", "Maximum Pressure - Operating": "175 psi"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 11:28:41.976', '2026-06-19 11:28:41.976'),
  ('c948e93b-3427-44b4-8af0-ce6db772ac9a', '7AC78', NULL, 'Supply Fan w/Drive Package: Belt Drive, 60 in Blade, Open Dripproof, 69,692 cfm, Cast, 3 ph', 'Belt-drive panel supply fans allow users to adjust the fans'' blade speed and airflow. Belt-drive fans are better suited than direct-drive fans for high air flow (≥ 2000 cfm) or high static pressure (≥ 0.50") applications. Belts connect the fans'' motors to their fan blades. These fans come with a drive package that includes a motor, pulleys, belts, and bushings, which saves time compared to purchasing all of these components separately.', NULL, '1444283e-0917-4137-9502-570d2dd92641', 'https://static.grainger.com/rp/s/is/image/Grainger/7AC78-M0000-1_v1', '3480228.00', NULL, 'in_stock', NULL, 'f', '7AC78', '{"Phase": "3", "Assembled": "Unassembled", "Drive Type": "Belt Drive", "Blade Diameter": "60 in", "Blade Material": "Aluminum", "Frame Material": "Steel", "Includes Motor": "Yes", "For Cut-Out Height": "62-1/2 in"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 11:28:42.009', '2026-06-19 11:28:42.009'),
  ('69d28230-f906-40ba-be7b-e880bc9451a4', '34KA13', NULL, 'Knit Sleeves: ANSI/ISEA Cut Level A4, Kevlar® with  Cut-Resistant, Black, XS, 1 PR', 'Medium-duty cut-resistant sleeves (ANSI A4-A5 cut levels) protect against cuts caused when performing automotive assembly and mining tasks, encountering sharp edges on ductwork, and handling recycling materials.', NULL, '140ae3c0-9071-4cbc-85e2-31b16b2c6d57', 'https://static.grainger.com/rp/s/is/image/Grainger/KBKB1T18-Top__J0R1_v4', '23914.00', NULL, 'in_stock', NULL, 'f', '34KA13', '{"Size": "XS", "Sleeve Type": "Elastic", "Sleeve Style": "Sleeve with Thumbhole", "Sleeve Length": "22 in", "Sleeve Features": "Cut-Resistant", "Sleeve Material": "Kevlar(R)", "ANSI/ISEA Cut Level": "A4", "ANSI/ISEA Heat Level": "2"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 11:28:42.046', '2026-06-19 11:28:42.046'),
  ('2b2b1dad-7639-4d89-91be-374419a8980e', '11D521', NULL, 'Slip-Fixed/Renewable Drill Bushing (SF): Std Wall, 1 23/64 in Inside Dia., 2 1/4 in Outside Dia.', 'These slip-fixed/renewable (SF) drill bushings come in standard sizes expressed in fractional inches. Standard-wall slip-fixed drill bushings have thicker walls and are typically sturdier than thin-wall slip-fixed drill bushings.', NULL, 'f0e0a1f9-a714-4aea-84c9-b5f100d3a0c5', 'https://static.grainger.com/rp/s/is/image/Grainger/11D260_AS01', '22847.00', NULL, 'in_stock', NULL, 'f', '11D521', '{"Drill Size": "1-23/64 in", "Inside Dia.": "1-23/64 in", "Bushing Code": "SF", "Outside Dia.": "2-1/4 in", "Bushing Head Type": "Headed", "Decimal Equivalent": "1.3594", "Measurement System": "Fractional Inch", "Drill Bushing Wall Type": "Standard Wall"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 11:28:43.067', '2026-06-19 11:28:43.067'),
  ('bdbdd17b-e8ea-4ab1-9ff7-e4ac413ff787', '36XH61', NULL, 'Jobber Length Drill Bit: #48, 118° 4-Facet Point, Solid Carbide', 'These general purpose solid carbide jobber-length drill bits for metal and plastic have regular spiral flutes that are best suited for nonchipping hard materials such as nonferrous metals, cast iron, and structural steel. Carbide drill bits provide excellent hardness, wear resistance, and heat resistance when drilling hard material. They are more durable than carbide-tipped bits when creating precision holes in hard materials, and are harder than high-speed steel and cobalt drill bits. Bright (Uncoated) drill bits can be resharpened and are a good choice when drilling soft materials such as aluminum and low-carbon steel. Jobber-Length drill bits are the most commonly used and provide a good balance of strength and accuracy when drilling into a variety of materials. Four-Facet Point drill bits have a chisel-type tip that is self-centering to reduce walking as the bit enters the workpiece, which eliminates the need to create a pilot hole, reduces required thrust, and creates a clean hole. Spiral Flute drill bits are used in most general purpose holemaking applications to effectively evacuate chips as they drill into the workpiece. Straight Shank drill bits have the same diameter along the length of the bit for high concentricity and minimal tool runout for high-performance drilling. 118 ° drill bits are general purpose, used for soft materials like wood and aluminum.', NULL, 'f0e0a1f9-a714-4aea-84c9-b5f100d3a0c5', 'https://static.grainger.com/rp/s/is/image/Grainger/36XE88_AS01', '8366.00', NULL, 'in_stock', NULL, 'f', '36XH61', '{"Point Type": "Four-Facet", "Flute Length": "7/8 in", "Finish/Coating": "Bright (Uncoated)", "Overall Length": "1-3/4 in", "Measurement System": "Wire", "Drill Bit Point Angle": "118  Degrees", "Size Decimal Equivalent": "0.0760", "Drill Bit Sizes Included": "#48"}', '{}', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-06-19 11:28:42.079', '2026-06-19 11:28:42.079'),
